a/HRx2QG7aoAEAhna.jpg?name=orig"}]},"reposted_by":true},{"id":"2090175850356322682","url":"https://x.com/steveschoger/status/2090175850356322682","author_handle":"steveschoger","reposted":false,"text":"My recently renovated kitchen\nhttps://x.com/TannerBuilds/status/2090100908566708658?s=20","created_at":"Wed Aug 19 20:35:30 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1787171730,"likes":348,"reposts":2,"replies":25,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":175,"views":60421,"is_note_tweet":false,"replying_to":null,"quote":{"id":"2090100908566708658","text":"One of my favorite kitchens I’ve seen in a long time.","author":"TannerBuilds","media_n":2},"media":null,"reposted_by":null},{"id":"2072021201774424147","url":"https://x.com/reinink/status/2072021201774424147","author_handle":"reinink","reposted":true,"text":"I'm doing something kind of interesting this week — I'm building a new template that @steveschoger designed in Figma a while back, but instead of writing it by hand this time, I'm getting Codex to build it for me.\n\nI'm building it one component at a time, and for each component, I'm giving it reference components that I previously wrote by hand.\n\nI provide the designs to the agent using the Figma Codex plugin. Steve always provides each component with at least five different breakpoints — so I provide all five at a time. This basically just involves including links to all the relevant frames in the Figma artboard.\n\nI also tell the agent to use any new components that we've created while building this new template — like buttons, containers, inputs, and things like that.\n\nAnd finally, I clean up the Tailwind classes using the \"canonicalize-tailwind\" skill that's included in @uidotsh. This just results in a little more idiomatic Tailwind code — like the code we would have written ourselves.\n\nI've tried the Figma Codex plugin before but wasn't super happy with the code that was generated. But giving it reference components that I previously wrote by hand — that's been a big unlock, and I'm getting much better results.\n\nThe AI journey continues! 🤖","created_at":"Tue Jun 30 18:15:25 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1782843325,"likes":38,"reposts":3,"replies":6,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":19,"views":7126,"is_note_tweet":true,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":{"all":[{"type":"photo","width":3400,"height":2276,"url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HMFLC9wXsAAFBo9.jpg?name=orig"}]},"reposted_by":true},{"id":"2041984965056057793","url":"https://x.com/reinink/status/2041984965056057793","author_handle":"reinink","reposted":true,"text":"It's been really exciting to see the first group of people using ui dot sh and getting better results from their agents! ✨\n\nWe've been sending out more invites over the last few days, but we're being careful not to bring too many people on at once, so it might take a couple of weeks to get them all out.\n\nAlso, a quick reminder to check your spam folder if you're waiting on one and haven't seen it yet.","created_at":"Wed Apr 08 21:02:08 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1775682128,"likes":19,"reposts":2,"replies":5,"quotes":0,"bookmarks":3,"views":9749,"is_note_tweet":true,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":null,"reposted_by":true},{"id":"2042272697283985610","url":"https://x.com/steveschoger/status/2042272697283985610","author_handle":"steveschoger","reposted":false,"text":"🎥 New video where I design a dashboard using Claude Code and Wispr Flow. \n\nOnce again, packed with tons of design tips 🔥","created_at":"Thu Apr 09 16:05:29 +0000 2026","created_timestamp":1775750729,"likes":760,"reposts":39,"replies":30,"quotes":3,"bookmarks":1261,"views":58983,"is_note_tweet":false,"replying_to":null,"quote":null,"media":{"all":[{"type":"video","width":1920,"height":1080,"duration":3685.589,"url":"https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2042270313203871744/vid/avc1/1920x1080/ziFGhqScQSt8ujr8.mp4?tag=21","thumbnail_url":"https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2042270313203871744/img/eYwLs41D8OxosRT4.jpg"}]},"reposted_by":